  "systemName": "Offsite Power and 13.8 kV Distribution",
  "systemAcronym": "OSP",
  "systemDescription": "<h3>Function</h3><p>The Offsite Power system (OSP) supplies the 13.8 kV plant switchgear from the transmission grid. It is the preferred\npower source for every AC load in HSMR-77: the two main feedwater pumps are fed directly from the 13.8 kV bus and the two 480 V\nsafety divisions (EPA, EPB) are fed through their load-center transformers.</p>\n<h3>Configuration</h3><ul><li>One 69 kV transmission line (on wood poles) into the switchyard, with a line circuit breaker.</li>\n<li>A 69 kV / 13.8 kV unit auxiliary transformer (UAT) in the switchyard.</li><li>An MV cable in a duct bank to the Electrical Building.</li>\n<li>The incoming breaker and the 13.8 kV switchgear bus in the 13.8 kV switchgear room (fire area EB_MV).</li></ul>\n<h3>Normal and emergency operation</h3><p>The circuit is always energized. On a loss of offsite power the 480 V divisions transfer\nautomatically to their battery energy storage systems (BESS) through their automatic transfer switches; the 13.8 kV loads (feedwater) are lost.\nThere are no diesel generators in the design.</p>\n<h3>Success criterion</h3><p>Every element of the single circuit works (series logic).</p>\n<h3>Evaluation cases</h3><p><b>72-h file:</b> probability that offsite power is lost during a 72-hour mission, no recovery credited.\n<b>1-yr file:</b> time-averaged unavailability over one year (failure rate &times; restoration time, 12 h for the grid, 168 h for the transformer).</p>\n<h3>Testing and maintenance</h3><p>Breakers are exercised during refuelling outages; the transformer is monitored continuously (dissolved gas, temperature).</p>\n<h3>Data</h3><p>Component data from the built-in NRC-INL 2020 parameter estimates; the grid LOOP rate and the cable rate are illustrative (HSMR-ILLUS).\nSeismic fragilities from NUREG/CR-4659 / NUREG/CR-3558 (the grid connection uses the ceramic-insulator fragility, Am = 0.2 g).\nFire: the UAT (NUREG-2169 bins 27 + 28) and the 13.8 kV switchgear bus (bin 15) can start fires; the breaker and bus fail in a fire in their room.</p>",
