      "systemLogic": [
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "# 480 VAC Division A (EPA): load center and MCC, fed from offsite power or from the Division A BESS",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "'''",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@source { HSMR-77-SDD Electrical section: each 480 V division has a load-center transformer fed from the 13.8 kV bus",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  and a battery energy storage system (BESS) behind an automatic transfer switch. There are no diesel generators. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@source { NRC-INL-2020 Transformer, bus, MCC, transfer switch, inverter and battery data. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@boundary { From the 13.8 kV feeder breaker (OSP supplies the bus) and from the BESS to the Division A MCC.",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  Load cables from the MCC are modeled in the systems that own the loads. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@basis { The division is powered when its load center and MCC work and either the offsite path or the BESS path works. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@assumption key { The BESS is sized for 72 hours of the Division A essential loads (charger, one CVCS pump,",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  one CCW pump and cooling-tower fan, one control room HVAC train). @input { HSMR-77-SDD: about 40 MWh usable energy. } }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@assumption verify { The BESS battery uses the NRC-INL 2020 station battery FTOP rate as a surrogate and the BESS fire",
