    {
      "id": "sys_hsmr_dca",
      "name": "125 VDC Division A",
      "acronym": "DCA",
      "description": "<h3>Function</h3><p>125 VDC Division A (DCA) is the highly reliable DC power supply of Division A: it powers the ESFAS Division A\nlogic and actuation relays, the shunt trip coil of reactor trip breaker A, and through ESFAS the ECCS and DHRS pilot solenoids of Division A.</p>\n<h3>Configuration</h3><ul><li>One 125 VDC battery sized for 72 hours of the division loads, with its battery cable.</li><li>One battery charger fed from the Division A MCC.</li>\n<li>One DC bus and one distribution panel, in the Division A DC room of the Control Building (separate fire area).</li></ul>\n<h3>Normal and emergency operation</h3><p>The charger carries the loads and floats the battery. On loss of AC the battery carries the loads for at least 72 hours.</p>\n<h3>Success criterion</h3><p>DC bus AND panel AND (battery path OR charger path with EPA power).</p>\n<h3>Evaluation cases</h3><p><b>72-h:</b> battery FTOP over 72 h (FM2). <b>1-yr:</b> battery in standby on float with a weekly check (FM3, &lambda;T/2); bus, panel and charger with repair (FM4).</p>\n<h3>Data</h3><p>NRC-INL 2020; DC cable rate illustrative. Fire: battery (NUREG-2169 bin 1), charger (bin 10) and DC bus (bin 15) are fire sources; everything in the room fails in a room fire.</p>",
      "sscsInSystem": [
        {
