          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@source { HSMR-77-SDD Electrical section: highly reliable DC power, two divisions, each battery sized for 72 hours. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@source { NRC-INL-2020 Battery, charger, DC bus and DC breaker data. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@boundary { From the battery and the charger (fed from the Division B MCC through EPB) to the Division B DC",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  distribution panel. Load cables belong to the systems that own the loads (ESA, RPS, ECCS, DHRS). }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@basis { DC is available when the bus and panel work and either the battery or the charger (with AC) supplies them. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@assumption key { The battery alone carries the Division B DC loads for 72 hours; no charger is needed in the mission. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@note { De-energize-to-trip loads (RTB undervoltage devices, channel bistables) go to their safe state on loss of DC;",
