    {
      "id": "sys_hsmr_sen",
      "name": "Protection Sensors (four channels)",
      "acronym": "SEN",
      "description": "<h3>Function</h3><p>The protection sensors (SEN) measure pressurizer pressure in four independent channels. Each channel's bistable\ntrips when pressure crosses its setpoint. Both RPS divisions and both ESFAS divisions vote the four channels 2-out-of-4.</p>\n<h3>Configuration</h3><ul><li>Four pressure transmitters on an instrument rack in the RXB piping gallery.</li>\n<li>Four separately routed channel signal cables to the Control Building.</li><li>Channel bistables: channels 1 and 3 in the Division A I&amp;C room, channels 2 and 4 in the Division B I&amp;C room.</li></ul>\n<h3>Success criterion</h3><p>At least 2 of the 4 channels produce a trip signal: <code>COMBINE(2, [CH-1], [CH-2], [CH-3], [CH-4])</code>.</p>\n<h3>Fail-safe behavior</h3><p>Channels are de-energize-to-trip, so loss of power or an open circuit trips the channel; those failure modes are excluded.</p>\n<h3>Common cause</h3><p>The four transmitters (and the four bistables) share templates, so the beta-factor model adds a CCF event for each group.</p>\n<h3>Evaluation cases</h3><p><b>72-h:</b> demand failure plus FTOP over 72 h. <b>1-yr:</b> demand failure plus FTOP with an 8-hour repair (channel checks every shift).</p>",
      "sscsInSystem": [
        {
          "id": 1790000000133,
