    {
      "id": "sys_hsmr_rps",
      "name": "Reactor Protection System",
      "acronym": "RPS",
      "description": "<h3>Function</h3><p>The Reactor Protection System (RPS) shuts the reactor down by interrupting power to the control rod drive mechanisms (CRDMs),\nwhich releases the 16 control rod assemblies into the core by gravity.</p>\n<h3>Configuration</h3><ul><li>Two trip divisions (A and B), each with digital 2-out-of-4 logic voting the four SEN channels, in the Division A / B I&amp;C rooms.</li>\n<li>Two reactor trip breakers (RTB-A, RTB-B) in series in the CRDM power supply; each has an undervoltage trip device (de-energize to trip) and a 125 VDC shunt trip coil (energize to trip).</li>\n<li>Trip signal cables from each division to its RTB; manual trip switches in the main control room with their own cables.</li>\n<li>16 CRDMs on the containment vessel head and 16 control rod assemblies.</li></ul>\n<h3>Success criterion</h3><p>(Division A OR Division B opens its RTB) AND at least 15 of 16 rods insert.</p>\n<h3>Human action</h3><p>RPS-HFE-MTRIP: the crew trips the reactor manually when the automatic trip fails (SPAR-H, diagnosis and action).</p>\n<h3>Dependencies</h3><p>SEN (sensors). DCA / DCB only for the shunt trip coils: on loss of DC the undervoltage devices trip the breakers.</p>\n<h3>Evaluation cases</h3><p>The CRDMs and rods use the standby model (FM3, rod-drop test every quarter) in both files, since they are needed only at the start.</p>\n<h3>Common cause</h3><p>Beta-factor CCF events are generated for the 16 CRDMs, the 16 rods, and the like components within RPS (e.g. the two RTBs).</p>",
      "sscsInSystem": [
        {
          "id": 1790000000161,
          "name": "RPS_PLC_PRES_A_TRIP",
