      "boundaryConditions": [],
      "systemLogic": [
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "# Reactor Protection System (RPS): two trip divisions, series reactor trip breakers and 16 control rods",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "'''",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@source { HSMR-77-SDD Module protection system: two RPS divisions vote the four sensor channels 2-out-of-4; each",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  division opens its own reactor trip breaker; the two RTBs are in series in the CRDM power supply. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@source { NRC-INL-2020 RTB, undervoltage and shunt trip device, PLC, CRD and control rod data. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@source { NUREG-CR-6883 SPAR-H worksheet for the manual trip action. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@boundary { From the four sensor channels (SEN) to the insertion of the control rods: division logic, trip signal",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  cables, the manual trip switches and their cables, both RTBs with their trip devices, the shunt trip DC supply and",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  the CRDMs and rods. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@basis { The reactor is shut down when at least 15 of the 16 rods insert and CRDM power is interrupted by either RTB. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@assumption key { Loss of CRDM power releases every rod; the RTBs are in series, so opening either one is enough. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@conservatism { The undervoltage device is credited only through its own failure mode; a loss of DC to the",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  undervoltage coil would trip the breaker (safe) and is not credited. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@modeler CLS 2026-10-13 { Rod-level logic with COMBINE(15 of 16). }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
