    {
      "id": "sys_hsmr_esa",
      "name": "ESFAS Division A",
      "acronym": "ESA",
      "description": "<h3>Function</h3><p>ESFAS Division A (ESA) generates the automatic actuation signals for the Division A trip solenoids of the ECCS valves,\nDHRS train A actuation valves and the Division A containment isolation valves.</p>\n<h3>Configuration</h3><ul><li>Digital 2-out-of-4 actuation logic and an output relay panel in the Division A I&amp;C room of the Control Building.</li>\n<li>125 VDC supply from DCA through its own cable.</li></ul>\n<h3>Success criterion</h3><p>SEN (2-out-of-4) AND logic AND relays AND DCA.</p>\n<h3>Design note</h3><p>Energize-to-actuate outputs (hypothetical design choice) make ESFAS depend on DC power; manual actuation from the\nmain control room is modeled in DHRS (with a SPAR-H human failure event).</p>\n<h3>Evaluation cases</h3><p>Demand failures in both files; the DC supply carries the time-dependent part.</p>",
