    {
      "id": "sys_hsmr_esb",
      "name": "ESFAS Division B",
      "acronym": "ESB",
      "description": "<h3>Function</h3><p>ESFAS Division B (ESB) generates the automatic actuation signals for the Division B trip solenoids of the ECCS valves,\nDHRS train B actuation valves and the Division B containment isolation valves.</p>\n<h3>Configuration</h3><ul><li>Digital 2-out-of-4 actuation logic and an output relay panel in the Division B I&amp;C room of the Control Building.</li>\n<li>125 VDC supply from DCB through its own cable.</li></ul>\n<h3>Success criterion</h3><p>SEN (2-out-of-4) AND logic AND relays AND DCB.</p>\n<h3>Design note</h3><p>Energize-to-actuate outputs (hypothetical design choice) make ESFAS depend on DC power; manual actuation from the\nmain control room is modeled in DHRS (with a SPAR-H human failure event).</p>\n<h3>Evaluation cases</h3><p>Demand failures in both files; the DC supply carries the time-dependent part.</p>",
      "sscsInSystem": [
        {
          "id": 1790000000265,
          "name": "ESB_PLC_PRES_B_ESF",
