      "systemLogic": [
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "# ESFAS Division B (ESB): automatic actuation of the Division B ECCS, DHRS and containment isolation",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "'''",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@source { HSMR-77-SDD Engineered safety features actuation system: two divisions, 2-out-of-4 voting, energize-to-actuate",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  outputs powered from 125 VDC Division B. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@source { NRC-INL-2020 PLC and relay data. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@boundary { From the sensor channels (SEN) to the Division B output relays, with the DC supply cable. The cables from",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  the relays to each actuated component belong to ECCS, DHRS and CIS. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@basis { A Division B actuation signal exists when 2 of 4 channels trip, the logic and the output relays work and",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  the division has DC power. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@assumption key { HSMR-77 uses energize-to-actuate pilot solenoids for ECCS and DHRS (no actuation on loss of DC), so",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  the actuation depends on DC power. This is a design choice of the hypothetical plant. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@modeler CLS 2026-10-13 { Division B ESFAS; manual actuation is modeled in the front-line systems. }",
