      "boundaryConditions": [],
      "systemLogic": [
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "# Emergency Core Cooling System (ECCS): three reactor vent valves and two recirculation valves",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "'''",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@source { HSMR-77-SDD ECCS: three reactor vent valves (RVV) on the RPV head and two reactor recirculation valves (RRV)",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  low on the RPV. Each valve opens when either of its two trip (pilot) solenoids, one per ESFAS division, opens. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@source { NRC-INL-2020 Hydraulic-operated and solenoid-operated valve data. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@boundary { The five main valves, their ten trip solenoids and actuation cables, and the containment vessel. Actuation",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  signals come from ESA and ESB; heat goes to the pool (UHS). }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@basis { Core cooling by ECCS needs at least one RVV open (steam vents to containment) and at least one RRV open",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "  (condensate returns to the RPV), with the containment vessel intact and the pool as the heat sink. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@assumption key { Energize-to-actuate pilots (hypothetical design choice): the ECCS valves do not open on loss of DC. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@conservatism { The inadvertent-actuation block and the pressure-dependent opening window are not credited or penalised. }",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "eol",
          "value": ";",
          "deletable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "comment",
          "value": "@modeler CLS 2026-10-13 { Valve-level logic, each valve with two divisional pilots. }",
          "deletable": true
