    {
      "id": "sys_hsmr_dhrs",
      "name": "Decay Heat Removal System",
      "acronym": "DHRS",
      "description": "<h3>Function</h3><p>The Decay Heat Removal System (DHRS) removes decay heat after a reactor trip when feedwater is lost, by natural circulation from\nthe steam generators to two passive condensers submerged in the reactor pool.</p>\n<h3>Configuration</h3><ul><li>Two trains (A on steam generator A, B on steam generator B). Each has a steam line, a passive condenser and a condensate line.</li>\n<li>Two parallel hydraulic actuation valves on each condensate line, each opened by a pilot solenoid energized by its ESFAS division.</li>\n<li>Manual actuation switches in the main control room for each train.</li></ul>\n<h3>Success criterion</h3><p>1 of 2 trains AND the pool (UHS). A train needs its actuation (ESFAS or manual), 1 of 2 actuation valves, its condenser and both lines.</p>\n<h3>Human action</h3><p>DHRS-HFE-MAN: the crew actuates DHRS manually when the automatic signal fails (SPAR-H; extra time available).</p>\n<h3>Leakage</h3><p>The steam and condensate lines have leak rates from LEAKRATE in the DHRS 3D script (per foot of the routed pipe), and rupture rates per foot in their template.</p>\n<h3>Evaluation cases</h3><p>Demand failures in both files; condenser and pipe rates over 72 h (72-h file) or with repair / restoration time (1-yr file).</p>",
      "sscsInSystem": [
        {
          "id": 1790000000325,
          "name": "DHRS_VALVE_HOV_A_AV1",
          "savedId": "DHRS-AV-A1",
          "description": "DHRS train A actuation valve 1 (opens the condensate return)",
          "label": "Hydraulic-Operated Valve (HOV)",
          "sscType": "Valve (VALVE)",
          "system": "Decay Heat Removal System",
          "uniqueLabel": "AV1",
          "trainId": "Train A",
          "moduleId": "",
          "templateId": "tpl_hsmr_hov",
          "source": {
            "id": "NRC-INL-2020",
            "name": "NRC-INL 2020 Parameter Estimation",
            "description": "Industry Average Parameter Estimates, 2020 Update, URL https://nrcoe.inl.gov/avgperf/"
          },
          "failureModes": [
            {
              "id": 1790000000007,
              "mode": "FTO",
              "probabilityType": "probability",
              "applicable": true,
              "failureModel": "0",
              "data": {
