    {
      "id": "sys_hsmr_ccw",
      "name": "Component Cooling Water System",
      "acronym": "CCW",
      "description": "<h3>Function</h3><p>Component Cooling Water (CCW) cools the CVCS makeup pumps (motor and seal coolers) and rejects the heat to a two-cell\nmechanical-draft cooling tower.</p>\n<h3>Configuration</h3><ul><li>Surge tank, two 100 % pumps (A running on Division A power, B standby on Division B power with auto-start), one heat exchanger\nand the supply / return headers in the Auxiliary Building CCW room.</li><li>Two cooling-tower cells outside, each with a fan (A running, B standby).</li></ul>\n<h3>Success criterion</h3><p>Tank AND HX AND headers AND (pump A or pump B train) AND (fan A or fan B train).</p>\n<h3>Leakage</h3><p>LEAKRATE on the surge tank and on the headers (per foot) in the CCW 3D script.</p>",
      "sscsInSystem": [
        {
          "id": 1790000000447,
          "name": "CCW_TANK_TANK",
          "savedId": "CCW-TNK",
          "description": "CCW surge tank",
