    {
      "id": "sys_hsmr_crv",
      "name": "Control Room HVAC (habitability)",
      "acronym": "CRV",
      "description": "<h3>Function</h3><p>The control room HVAC (CRV) keeps the main control room habitable: it cools the room and, on an isolation signal, closes the\noutside-air intake and recirculates through the emergency filtration unit.</p>\n<h3>Configuration</h3><p>Two 100 % trains in separate Control Building HVAC rooms (separate fire areas): AHU and chiller A (running, Division A) with the HEPA / charcoal\nfiltration unit and outside-air isolation damper 1, and AHU and chiller B (standby, Division B, auto-start) with damper 2. The two dampers are in series in the outside-air intake.</p>\n<h3>Success criterion</h3><p>(Train A OR train B) AND filter AND (damper 1 OR damper 2 closes).</p>\n<h3>Evaluation cases</h3><p><b>72-h:</b> running train over 72 h, standby train start and run. <b>1-yr:</b> running train with repair; standby train start and TM.</p>",
      "sscsInSystem": [
        {
          "id": 1790000000482,
